# Human Mode's strength by rating (src/human.snail, hn_choose), at each knot of CheckElo:
#   CheckTemperature: a multiple of Human Temperature (above 1 noisier and weaker);
#   CheckPenalty: each candidate's weight times exp(-penalty * the expected score it gives away);
#   CheckNodes: the check's search budget, a multiple of Human Check Nodes;
#   CheckMaxLoss: candidates giving away more are dropped (1.0: none);
#   CheckNetElo: the rating the net is told (part of the measured configuration);
#   CheckTail: the share of weight kept by moves outside the check's candidates (1: all moves);
#   CheckMoves: how many of the net's top moves the check searches;
#   CheckBlunder: the share of moves played as a beginner's blunder (Human Blunder).
# Calibrated on the Lichess blitz scale by tools/human/ladder_cal.py (Maia bots pinned at their
# long-run ratings, neighbour games along one strength path). Generated; do not edit.

